## Scientific Principle

Each representation is introduced only when the preceding representation becomes insufficient to answer the next scientific question.

Semantic understanding therefore emerges progressively rather than being explicitly imposed.

---

## Figure Caption (Draft)

Figure 3.1. Emergence of the Semantic Language of Fashion Sketches. The proposed framework progressively transforms continuous garment geometry into increasingly expressive scientific representations. Each representation addresses a distinct scientific question while preserving explicit traceability to the underlying garment geometry. Semantic understanding emerges through the interaction of learned geometric, structural, morphological, contextual, and semantic representations rather than through predefined semantic annotations.

